With legs trembling

02:03.880 --> 02:07.140
Hirakinaotte arinomama GO!
I get serious and just go for it!

02:07.510 --> 02:10.139
Zenkai, soukai, daitenkai Recuperation,
exhilaration, a big revolution

02:10.140 --> 02:13.180
Nandemo chokushin STRAIGHT
No matter what, keep heading straight

02:13.520 --> 02:16.189
Sekai, mankai, mugendai
The world, in full bloom, infinity

02:16.190 --> 02:19.729
Kyou mo genki ni koko ni imasu (HEY!) I'm
here again today, living to the fullest (Hey!)

02:19.730 --> 02:21.246
Ippai hibike MUSIC
Ring out, tons of music

02:21.270 --> 02:22.689
Ippai kimari POSING
Do tons of cool posing

02:22.690 --> 02:24.336
Ippai todoke FEELING?
Let tons of feelings reach you

02:24.360 --> 02:25.609
Super Soni let's go!
Super Soni let's go!

02:25.610 --> 02:27.279
Suggoi shigeki tenkomori
Stimulation super piling up

02:27.280 --> 02:28.619
Suggoi tama ni karamawari
Sometimes super running in circles

02:28.620 --> 02:30.426
Suggoi kimi to zutto ENJOY
Always super enjoy being with you

02:30.450 --> 02:32.620
SUPER SONI LET'S GO! Desu
Super Soni let's go! Yes

02:35.080 --> 02:36.830
Musashino French restaurant map...

02:36.831 --> 02:38.670
Musashino Publications

02:38.671 --> 02:43.510
Musashino B-grade gourmet guide... Musashino
"weekly map." It's all stuff we've done before.

02:44.010 --> 02:47.469
What else is a local town
mag supposed to cover?

02:47.470 --> 02:49.509
We've gotta change things up...

02:49.510 --> 02:53.770
Do somethin' flashy that won't break the
budget. There must be something, right?

02:53.970 --> 02:55.559
There he goes again, talking out of his...

02:55.560 --> 02:56.560
Hey, Chief!

02:56.570 --> 03:04.570
Entrusting
sentiments
to the
setting
sun
.
.
.

02:57.140 --> 02:59.189
How about this Super Sonico girl?

02:59.190 --> 03:02.900
Her profile says she's attending
Musasaka University of Science.

03:03.360 --> 03:08.109
I think an in-depth story on a local college student
who's also a bikini model could have some pull.

03:08.110 --> 03:10.239
You sure you don't just want to meet her?

03:10.240 --> 03:12.779
That sounds good. What's her name again?

03:12.780 --> 03:16.410
It's "Sonico." Maybe we could have
her do a bikini shoot for us, too.

03:17.080 --> 03:19.709
Okay. Sayaka, you're the lead on this.

03:19.710 --> 03:20.170
Huh?

03:20.710 --> 03:23.300
Both of you being girls
kinda makes it better, right?

03:23.500 --> 03:25.259
But... No way!

03:25.260 --> 03:29.130
I don't want to work with some self-obsessed
girl who's out there doing swimsuit shoots!

03:26.430 --> 03:29.129
MAP OF JAPAN

03:29.130 --> 03:34.139
Well, that's the privilege of being young, right?
You probably couldn't pull it off anymore...

03:34.140 --> 03:34.930
Shut up.

03:34.931 --> 03:37.770
Anyway, try to set up an
appointment with her agency.

03:38.020 --> 03:38.940
But I...

03:38.941 --> 03:43.229
Editor's orders. And be sure not to
go over the usual budget, 'kay?

03:43.230 --> 03:45.690
Dammit! Must be nice, Saya.

03:46.820 --> 03:48.780
Our print run is just 2,000 copies.

03:49.110 --> 03:53.530
Like a talent agency would want to deal with
some piddling town mag with no budget...

03:57.000 --> 04:02.580
I'm grateful that you contacted our agency.
I am Kitamura, Super Sonico's manager.

04:02.790 --> 04:08.220
Ah! How do you do? My name is Super Sonico.
It's a pleasure to meet with you today!

04:08.880 --> 04:13.639
The pleasure's mine. How do you do? I'm
Sayaka Kinomoto of Musashino Publications.

04:13.640 --> 04:14.760
Please, be seated.

04:15.140 --> 04:16.430
Thanks very much.

04:17.220 --> 04:19.390
I can't believe they called me here.

04:19.810 --> 04:23.900
If they were going to say no,
I'd have preferred they just hung up on me!

04:24.560 --> 04:26.150
Anyway, what the heck?

04:26.320 --> 04:29.320
This is the first time I've
seen a bikini model up close.

04:29.860 --> 04:32.450
Small brains and big boobs.

04:32.740 --> 04:36.280
But she's skinny! And her skin's so moist,
without any makeup!

04:36.790 --> 04:39.410
Long eyelashes... Gorgeous hair...!

04:40.370 --> 04:41.080
Anyway...

04:41.081 --> 04:42.119
Um, yes?

04:42.120 --> 04:47.419
About this "town magazine" your company
publishes doing an in-depth article on Sonico...

04:47.420 --> 04:51.840
Here we go. If he wanted to say no,
he didn't have to do it face-to-face!

04:52.220 --> 04:53.969
By all means. It'd be our pleasure.

04:53.970 --> 04:54.970
Huh?

04:55.050 --> 04:58.969
I'm honored that a magazine that talks
about the area would want to feature me!

04:58.970 --> 05:00.600
I really look forward to it!

05:00.890 --> 05:02.439
Y-you don't mind?

05:02.440 --> 05:05.940
In this day and age, local coverage
has become the norm.

05:06.360 --> 05:09.230
Local gourmets... Local heroes...

05:09.400 --> 05:11.740
Local anime, local mascots...

05:11.950 --> 05:13.610
And local celebrities.

05:14.200 --> 05:19.870
We're well aware how vital it is to have
the love and support of our fellow locals.

05:20.040 --> 05:24.539
It will be an in-depth piece,
so it will cover your private life, too.

05:24.540 --> 05:27.750
No problem. I've already
cleaned up my place!

05:28.000 --> 05:30.509
Um, that's not really what I meant...

05:30.510 --> 05:32.420
There's no need for concern.

05:33.130 --> 05:39.720
On the contrary, I want people to know Sonico
as she truly is, not some fabricated image.

05:40.390 --> 05:45.149
There might be times I ask you NOT to
accompany us in the interview process...

05:45.150 --> 05:49.320
Well, it can't be helped. As you're both
ladies, there shouldn't be any problem.

05:49.480 --> 05:52.319
Of course, we shall review the
article prior to publication...

05:52.320 --> 05:53.649
Well, of course.

05:53.650 --> 05:56.359
In that case, I leave Sonico in your care.

05:56.360 --> 05:58.070
Thank you very much!

05:59.580 --> 06:01.909
I got permission for
the Super Sonico story.

06:01.910 --> 06:05.120
Right. We start the day after
tomorrow, for two days and one night.

06:05.790 --> 06:07.040
Thanks very much.

06:12.460 --> 06:13.460
Hello?

06:13.670 --> 06:15.380
Hey there. It's me.

06:18.760 --> 06:20.140
Sorry, Yuuko.

06:20.680 --> 06:21.390
Waiting long?

06:21.391 --> 06:23.599
No. Just got here myself.

06:23.600 --> 06:26.639
I haven't been to Roppongi
in so long, I got lost.

06:26.640 --> 06:29.860
Sorry 'bout that. You
like Cassis Oolong, right?

06:30.230 --> 06:31.150
What? No booze.

06:31.151 --> 06:33.739
Where's the harm? It's been a while
since we've seen each other.

06:33.740 --> 06:35.240
Stay and talk with me.

06:37.530 --> 06:40.909
Okay, here's to the reunion
of the only two female editors

06:40.910 --> 06:44.160
from Literary Dept. 3 of the
Yamakawa Shoten group.

06:49.580 --> 06:52.050
So, you're an editor at
a town magazine now?

06:52.500 --> 06:55.089
Still just a temp. And you?

06:55.090 --> 06:57.970
No change. Still at Literary Dept. 3.

06:58.090 --> 07:01.299
But that's great. Being full
time at a major company...

07:01.300 --> 07:07.190
Don't be jealous. I went through hell before
getting the job I wanted, as a novel editor.

07:07.390 --> 07:10.109
Still, my authors are so spoiled.

07:10.110 --> 07:14.320
They eat and drink what they want,
then claim the expenses like it's nothing!

07:14.570 --> 07:18.150
They get drunk, feel me up,
make passes at me... It's the worst!

07:18.410 --> 07:20.910
Seriously, they can all go to hell!

07:21.450 --> 07:23.989
You drunk already? That's pretty fast.

07:23.990 --> 07:28.080
Well, of course I'm not.
Anyway, how's work at your town mag?

07:28.210 --> 07:31.250
I'm doing an in-depth story
on some local bikini model.

07:31.750 --> 07:35.339
Pretty funky for a town
mag. Was that your idea?

07:35.340 --> 07:36.710
No, no way!

07:37.050 --> 07:42.600
It's like they have ulterior motives, or are
just trying random stuff to see what works.

07:43.300 --> 07:45.640
Like me, to be honest...

07:46.770 --> 07:49.810
You're not writing anymore? Your novel?

07:50.400 --> 07:51.940
I gave it up long ago.

07:52.190 --> 07:53.400
I don't have the talent.

07:55.900 --> 07:58.450
Excuse me! The wine list, please.

08:00.700 --> 08:01.989
Come on.

08:01.990 --> 08:05.410
Saya, get a grip. Hey!

08:05.740 --> 08:07.830
Yeah, I know...

08:08.960 --> 08:10.209
Where are your keys?

08:10.210 --> 08:14.170
My pocket, somewhere! Look for 'em.

08:26.640 --> 08:28.480
"Gave it up long ago," huh?

08:29.810 --> 08:31.440
You haven't changed a bit.

08:34.400 --> 08:37.440
You're just like you were then, Saya.

08:40.950 --> 08:43.489
Interviewing this early in the morning?

08:43.490 --> 08:46.030
Working for a magazine is hard, huh?

08:46.700 --> 08:50.619
Sorry about this. I rang the doorbell,
but there was no answer.

08:50.620 --> 08:51.789
Yes, I'm sure.

08:51.790 --> 08:52.790
Huh?

08:53.540 --> 08:56.210
This will be tough, but
please do your best.

08:59.880 --> 09:02.680
Well then, I'll leave you to it.

09:02.970 --> 09:03.970
Huh?

09:19.440 --> 09:24.410
This isn't what I was
expecting. It looks so normal.

09:30.620 --> 09:31.620
Still...

09:35.080 --> 09:38.000
How can she sleep through
all these alarm clocks?

09:40.760 --> 09:42.920
This is your punishment.

09:49.600 --> 09:53.269
Sonico. Sonico, it's already past 8:30!

09:53.270 --> 09:56.519
Come on, you're going to
be late for school. SONICO!

09:56.520 --> 10:00.689
I'm up... Finished eating... I'll be back.

10:00.690 --> 10:01.530
She's going to school in her dreams...
I'm up... Finished eating... I'll be back.

10:01.531 --> 10:03.051
She's going to school in her dreams...

10:14.370 --> 10:16.120
You're finally up!

10:17.250 --> 10:18.750
Miss Kinomoto!

10:20.630 --> 10:23.380
I'm sorry. But this is
part of the article, so...

10:26.180 --> 10:29.509
H-hey! Don't go back to sleep. Just get up!

10:29.510 --> 10:32.060
C'mon! C'mon! C'mon! C'mon!

10:34.680 --> 10:38.900
Miss Kinomoto... Thank you very much.

10:39.150 --> 10:40.819
Yeah, just get going.

10:40.820 --> 10:43.399
Right. Yes, I understand!

10:43.400 --> 10:45.530
Yeah!

10:46.950 --> 10:48.319
What is her deal?

10:48.320 --> 10:53.910
Being that hard to wake up isn't normal.
Well, time to get my things and...

10:54.660 --> 10:58.960
Wait, no! Wait, Sonico!
I'm coming to school, too!

10:59.670 --> 11:01.000
Wait up!

11:07.630 --> 11:08.970
Super Sonico.

11:09.390 --> 11:14.350
University freshman. Studying marine
biology at Musa-Sakari University.

11:14.720 --> 11:17.890
Height: 158 cm. Blood type: A.

11:18.600 --> 11:22.770
Likes hot baths, playing
with cats, and video games.

11:23.860 --> 11:26.900
Favorite foods: ramen and macarons.

11:29.070 --> 11:32.490
It's all just so... normal.

11:33.330 --> 11:35.410
It's not at all how I pictured her.

11:35.870 --> 11:37.830
Super Sonico?

11:38.120 --> 11:39.329
This is her.

11:39.330 --> 11:41.749
Oh, the one who's always late for class.

11:41.750 --> 11:42.840
Oh, her!

11:43.750 --> 11:47.840
We have some liberal arts classes together.
She gets good grades.

11:49.430 --> 11:51.679
So she's a bikini model?

11:51.680 --> 11:53.969
I knew she had good fashion sense, but...

11:53.970 --> 11:58.230
She's a bikini model, yet she makes
THIS little of an impression?

12:02.060 --> 12:05.020
The client has given permission for
you to cover the shoot.

12:05.230 --> 12:06.610
Thank you very much.

12:11.660 --> 12:14.120
Sonico! Look over here next!

12:14.700 --> 12:18.079
Yes, that's it. Put a hand
on your hip. Yes, that's good.

12:18.080 --> 12:19.080
Here goes.

12:21.920 --> 12:23.460
Is the article going well?

12:24.090 --> 12:25.130
Yes, I suppose...

12:26.460 --> 12:29.379
Sorry, but may I ask you a question?

12:29.380 --> 12:30.380
Please.

12:31.180 --> 12:35.220
Why do you think Sonico's
trying to be a model?

12:36.560 --> 12:40.770
It's just... She doesn't
seem like the type.

12:42.270 --> 12:46.110
Then please ask her that yourself.

12:47.940 --> 12:50.070
I think that belongs in the article, too.

12:55.990 --> 12:59.159
The reason I work part
time as a bikini model?

12:59.160 --> 13:00.160
Yes.

13:00.790 --> 13:07.089
Well, I started because one of my
dad's friends asked me to give it a try.

13:07.090 --> 13:09.090
I was unsure at first...

13:09.760 --> 13:12.930
but I guess it was my first
step toward independence.

13:14.340 --> 13:16.349
So you gave it a shot.

13:16.350 --> 13:21.180
Yes. I just went, like, "Yeah!"
and totally took the plunge.

13:21.850 --> 13:24.060
What was your first shoot like?

13:24.730 --> 13:27.770
I was... extremely embarrassed.

13:28.190 --> 13:33.109
But everyone was there, from the client
who'd chosen me and all the staff,

13:33.110 --> 13:38.700
to my manager and my grandma, who came
to cheer me on, so I had to do my best.

13:39.660 --> 13:40.660
That's how I felt.

13:43.330 --> 13:49.089
So, is it your dream now to become
a famous bikini model?

13:49.090 --> 13:51.800
Um, no. Actually...

13:52.380 --> 13:53.800
My dream...

13:54.470 --> 13:55.470
is THIS!

13:55.760 --> 13:57.009
The guitar?

13:57.010 --> 13:58.470
Yes. Rock-and-roll!

13:59.760 --> 14:00.770
Nice to meet you!

14:01.020 --> 14:05.520
We're the three-piece girl band
First Astronomical Velocity!

14:06.850 --> 14:09.480
On bass, I'm Suzu
Fujimi, the leader. Thanks!

14:09.900 --> 14:13.689
On drums, I'm Fuuri
Watanuki. Nice to meet you.

14:13.690 --> 14:16.859
Um, sorry to disturb
your practice like this.

14:16.860 --> 14:19.580
Not at all. Follow us and
write as much as you like!

14:19.870 --> 14:21.949
By all means, make people want
to come to our regular shows

14:21.950 --> 14:24.999
and see Nico's wild
guitar-playing in person!

14:25.000 --> 14:27.329
Uh, Suzu? You're way too hyper.

14:27.330 --> 14:31.130
Oh, you'll need some pictures, right?
To the studio, everyone. Go, go!

14:31.750 --> 14:32.960
Love and...

14:33.300 --> 14:34.720
Peace!

14:36.880 --> 14:39.640
Why are YOU in the shot too, Aako?!

14:40.180 --> 14:41.599
It just seemed right.

14:41.600 --> 14:42.520
Um, Suzu? Shouldn't we start practice?

14:42.521 --> 14:44.229
And what's with the flawless makeup?
Um, Suzu? Shouldn't we start practice?

14:44.230 --> 14:45.939
On the prowl? Looking for a hubby?

14:45.940 --> 14:47.139
N-no friggin' way!

14:47.140 --> 14:48.100
Mayoikonda semai rojiura no noraneko
A stray cat in a narrow alleyway

14:48.101 --> 14:51.230
Mayoikonda semai rojiura no noraneko
A stray cat in a narrow alleyway

14:52.480 --> 14:56.860
Tsumannai yo, shakai no RULE ni tameiki
It's so dull, I sigh at society's rules

14:57.740 --> 14:59.720
Teki wa dare da?
Who's the enemy?

14:59.721 --> 15:01.080
Nico's good points?

15:01.240 --> 15:03.535
Asu o ikinuku tame
To live to see tomorrow

15:03.536 --> 15:06.460
When I'm with her, I have so much
fun that I forget I'm hungry.

15:05.870 --> 15:07.920
Michi-naki michi e
We take the road with no path

15:07.921 --> 15:12.920
Well, it's hard for me to put it simply,
but this much I can say—Nico is...

15:08.370 --> 15:12.340
BELIEVE MYSELF, ima sugu ni koko kara
Believe myself, starting now, going forward

15:12.550 --> 15:17.510
Namida wa misenaide shinjita basho e I'll show
no tears and head for the place I've believed in

15:13.500 --> 15:14.669
mine! All mine!

15:14.670 --> 15:15.670
Huh?!

15:16.970 --> 15:19.345
No fair. You can't
have her all to yourself!

15:19.346 --> 15:22.970
Tsukamitore, mamorinuke, kanarazu Grasp
for it, protect it, and without a doubt

15:23.260 --> 15:28.560
Boku wa mada shiranai kedo
I don't know everything yet, but

15:29.270 --> 15:30.610
Tatakaunda!
I'll fight!

15:31.360 --> 15:32.485
ZEPPELIN

15:32.486 --> 15:33.610
PUB

15:34.030 --> 15:35.740
YAAAY!

15:36.360 --> 15:37.609
Um...

15:37.610 --> 15:40.359
I'm sorry, but she's covering me...

15:40.360 --> 15:41.779
Don't bother them.

15:41.780 --> 15:43.869
We ain't no bother!

15:43.870 --> 15:47.620
That reporter said we should
just act normal and stuff!

15:47.750 --> 15:49.370
So, as always...

15:50.210 --> 15:51.789
YAAAY!

15:51.790 --> 15:54.089
I'm very sorry, Miss Kinomoto.

15:54.090 --> 15:55.129
It's okay.

15:55.130 --> 15:56.170
Say, Miss?

15:58.720 --> 16:00.130
Please, have a drink.

16:00.470 --> 16:00.840
Mr. Yasu, no saké!

16:00.841 --> 16:02.389
I'm working, so...
Mr. Yasu, no saké!

16:02.390 --> 16:04.259
Don't be shy.
It's our treat!

16:04.260 --> 16:06.220
Where's the harm?
You can hold your liquor, right?

16:06.520 --> 16:08.480
Everyone, you're being bad!

16:13.060 --> 16:14.229
Miss Kinomoto!

16:14.230 --> 16:16.150
Lady, you rock!
Yo, bring us some snacks!

16:18.530 --> 16:22.199
Hey, Leyla! Another beer for Miss Reporter!

16:22.200 --> 16:23.410
Thanks a lot.

16:25.990 --> 16:28.909
I'm very sorry. Tomi and his friends are...

16:28.910 --> 16:31.999
No, it's on me. I should've been working.

16:32.000 --> 16:34.839
Um, yes, there's that as well!

16:34.840 --> 16:35.500
I'm sorry.

16:35.500 --> 16:36.380
No at all!

16:36.381 --> 16:40.169
Sonico, we have an early start tomorrow,
so you should take a bath.

16:40.170 --> 16:41.719
Huh? No, I'm...

16:41.720 --> 16:45.299
You're a bikini model, so you have
to take care of your skin.

16:45.300 --> 16:47.310
Okay, thank you.

16:48.600 --> 16:51.480
Well, I'll jump in and jump right back out!

16:51.810 --> 16:54.060
No, just take your time.

16:57.400 --> 17:01.280
Miss Kinomoto, relax a little
till you're back up to speed.

17:17.800 --> 17:20.010
Aim for the future

17:21.760 --> 17:22.969
Lyrics?

17:22.970 --> 17:26.509
Aim for the future

17:26.510 --> 17:27.640
The future...

17:36.810 --> 17:38.480
M-Miss Kinomoto!

17:39.780 --> 17:41.030
Got some good ones.

17:41.740 --> 17:43.149
You're still drunk, huh?

17:43.150 --> 17:44.699
This is an IN-DEPTH article!

17:44.700 --> 17:45.989
But you can't!

17:45.990 --> 17:48.410
This is... Y-you can't!

17:52.870 --> 17:53.870
Just kidding.

17:54.540 --> 17:56.920
I'll delete them, so don't worry.

17:58.130 --> 17:59.130
Um...

17:59.500 --> 18:01.670
Are you okay, Miss Kinomoto?

18:03.340 --> 18:08.510
Hey, Sonico. Suppose... Just suppose,
what if your band never gets popular?

18:08.970 --> 18:14.940
If people say it's no good,
that you have no talent...

18:15.310 --> 18:18.060
But your bikini modeling works out.

18:20.190 --> 18:24.820
If that happened...
Would you quit the band?

18:27.740 --> 18:29.660
I don't think I would.

18:31.120 --> 18:32.200
Why not?

18:33.540 --> 18:39.250
Because I like it. I love rock, and
I've always wanted to have a band.

18:39.540 --> 18:40.750
My wish has come true.

18:41.420 --> 18:45.670
Of course it would be great
to be a professional musician.

18:46.010 --> 18:52.560
But even if that doesn't happen,
I've gotten so much power from rock.

18:52.970 --> 18:57.600
Now, I'd like to give that same
power to everyone who hears us.

18:58.440 --> 19:03.820
I want to keep making the rock I
love with Suzu and Fuuri.

19:05.950 --> 19:09.320
I'm sorry. I must have
sounded full of myself.

19:11.120 --> 19:12.240
Miss Kinomoto?

19:18.870 --> 19:23.590
How nice for her. To be having fun,
surrounded by good will...

19:23.840 --> 19:29.930
But that's because she's still young. She hasn't
gone out into the world, had it reject her.

19:30.300 --> 19:32.810
She can say that because
she hasn't hit the wall yet!

19:34.720 --> 19:39.939
Just getting by takes everything you've
got, and you lose so much along the way...

19:39.940 --> 19:41.730
Still, you can't give up.

19:46.570 --> 19:48.490
You want to keep doing
it because you like it...

19:49.160 --> 19:51.160
That's just common sense, isn't it?!

19:51.450 --> 19:54.910
What the hell am I doing?!
I haven't accomplished anything!

19:55.450 --> 19:58.540
There's nothing I could
say to that girl. Nothing!

19:59.790 --> 20:05.000
I love it, so I should do
it! Why can't I?! WHY?!

20:13.890 --> 20:17.680
Aim for the future

20:25.900 --> 20:27.110
Good morning, Sonico.

20:27.610 --> 20:28.989
I'll take you to school.

20:28.990 --> 20:30.149
Miss Kinomoto...

20:30.150 --> 20:31.490
Just call me Saya.

20:32.320 --> 20:33.820
It's more informal, right?

20:36.490 --> 20:38.159
I hope to get some
more good material today.

20:38.160 --> 20:41.830
Oh, yes. I look forward to it, too.

20:43.960 --> 20:45.499
Thank you, Sonico.

20:45.500 --> 20:46.300
Huh?

20:46.301 --> 20:50.090
I guess you could say...
You gave me some power.

20:51.130 --> 20:53.679
So... I'm grateful!

20:53.680 --> 20:55.300
Huh? Uh...

20:55.720 --> 21:00.429
Never mind. But thanks.
Okay, let's do our best today!

21:00.430 --> 21:03.310
R-right! YEAH!

21:23.920 --> 21:27.840
Tooku de kirakira hikaru
They shine, sparkling in the distance

21:29.300 --> 21:33.930
Toutei te ga todokanakute
And are so far out of reach

21:37.260 --> 21:41.020
Yume o akiramenai koto
Not giving up on those dreams

21:42.560 --> 21:47.980
Sonna ni kantan na koto ja nai
Isn't such an easy thing

21:48.360 --> 21:54.240
Toki ni wa nakitakunaru yo
Sometimes, you'll want to cry

21:54.780 --> 21:57.240
Iya ni natte You hate it all

21:57.620 --> 22:02.370
Tebanasu koto mo aru kedo
And there are times you'll give up on them

22:02.660 --> 22:07.670
Kakudo o kaetara sugu soko ni But then you
change direction and they're right there

22:09.710 --> 22:14.470
Hohoeminagara temaneite
Beckoning you with a smile

22:15.930 --> 22:21.180
"Ganbarimashita" to itte kureru
"You've worked hard," they'll say

22:21.350 --> 22:24.520
Ashita ga aru koto
Because I want to believe

22:24.730 --> 22:27.650
Ashita ga aru koto
Because I want to believe

22:28.110 --> 22:31.940
Shinjiteitai kara
There is a tomorrow

22:37.740 --> 22:40.950
I read the article. It looks wonderful.

22:41.290 --> 22:43.200
Yes, even better than hoped.

22:43.700 --> 22:46.790
You wrote an honest article about
Sonico as she truly is.

22:46.791 --> 22:48.270
Rock is my dream

22:48.271 --> 22:51.919
This is the kind of article I wanted
to read. I'm genuinely thankful to you.

22:51.920 --> 22:52.920
And I to you.

22:53.090 --> 22:55.880
Thank you very much. If you'll excuse me.

23:00.510 --> 23:02.890
Hello? Yuuko? It's me.

23:03.430 --> 23:07.140
Huh? Sorry, no. Gotta pass on drinks.

23:07.940 --> 23:10.440
I think I'll start writing
something new today.

23:11.900 --> 23:14.740
Yes, of course I will.

23:17.910 --> 23:19.030
Because...

23:20.070 --> 23:21.490
I love novels!

23:24.960 --> 23:32.960
Next Episode Preview

23:25.410 --> 23:29.039
That's incredible, Ouka!
You landed a TV commercial!

23:29.040 --> 23:31.630
At last, the Age of Ouka has begun!

23:31.750 --> 23:33.670
And the presentation is
on a super luxury liner!

23:33.750 --> 23:37.010
Will you come too, Sonico?
I want you to see me at my best!

23:37.020 --> 23:39.980
Cruising of the Dead

23:37.510 --> 23:39.760
Next time: "Cruising of the Dead."
